## Purpose and baseline

This is {{NAME}}'s living execution plan and the current plan for this repository. It tracks product and repository work; the [README](../../README.md), current policies, and [accepted ADRs](../adr/README.md) still govern implementation.

{{NAME}} was initialized on {{DATE}} from {{FOUNDATION_NAME}} commit `{{BASELINE}}` of {{FOUNDATION_URL}}. The [project manifest](../../.orion/project.json) records that immutable initialization commit and the {{FOUNDATION_NAME}} baseline currently integrated.

The inherited [{{FOUNDATION_NAME}} foundation plan](../implementation-plan.md) records how {{FOUNDATION_NAME}} itself was built: its completed phases, maintenance tasks, and conditional Phase 12 describe the {{FOUNDATION_NAME}} repository at their recorded evidence. They are not tasks of this project, and their completed statuses do not certify this repository. The same applies to the [{{FOUNDATION_NAME}} human-action checklist](../human-actions.md) and [foundation acceptance report](../foundation-acceptance.md). Do not edit those foundation files to track {{NAME}}; they continue to receive {{FOUNDATION_NAME}} upgrades.

## Maintaining this plan

Apply the [maintenance rules and status vocabulary](../implementation-plan.md#maintaining-this-plan) of the {{FOUNDATION_NAME}} plan to this plan and to the [project human actions](human-actions.md). Allocate stable task IDs as `PJ-NN`; never reuse or renumber them. Record evidence produced for this repository—local validation, this repository's CI runs, and this repository's external settings—rather than {{FOUNDATION_NAME}}'s.

## Inherited foundation

{{NAME}} inherits {{FOUNDATION_NAME}}'s architecture, policies, accepted ADRs, validation gate, generated references, Living Documentation Portal, and developer workflow at the recorded baseline. They are usable immediately, but a result recorded in {{FOUNDATION_NAME}}'s evidence is not a result for this repository until it passes in this checkout and in this repository's CI.

The `@orion/*` package scope, `ORION_*` configuration names, `orion_*` token claims, and the `Orion required gate` CI check name are the foundation namespace, not the product brand. Keeping them avoids rename conflicts in every {{FOUNDATION_NAME}} upgrade; rename them only through a deliberate decision under PJ-05.

